Presidential elections were held in [[Romania]] on 10 November 2019, with a second round held on 24 November 2019.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Presidential election timetable approved |url=https://www.romania-insider.com/romania-presidential-election-2019-timetable |website=Romania Insider |access-date=2026-07-16}}</ref> They were the eighth presidential election held in [[Romanian Revolution|post-1989]] Romania. Incumbent [[President of Romania|president]] [[Klaus Iohannis]], first elected in the [[2014 Romanian presidential election|2014 election]], was eligible for re-election.

In the first round, Iohannis finished first with 37.82% of the vote, while former [[Prime Minister of Romania|prime minister]] and ex-leader of the [[Social Democratic Party (Romania)|Social Democratic Party]] (PSD), [[Viorica Dăncilă]], finished second with 22.26%. As no candidate received an absolute majority, the two advanced to the second round.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Presidential elections in Romania: BEC first round final results |url=https://www.romania-actualitati.ro/news-in-english/presidential-elections-in-romania-bec-first-round-final-results-id128657.html |website=Radio România Actualități |date=2019-11-14 |access-date=2026-07-16}}</ref>

In the second round, Iohannis defeated Dăncilă in a landslide, receiving 66.09% of the vote to her 33.91%. It was the third-highest vote share in a Romanian presidential election since 1989, behind only [[Ion Iliescu]], who received 85.07% of the vote in [[1990 Romanian general election|1990]] and 66.83% in [[2000 Romanian general election|2000]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Alegerile prezidențiale din România, perioada 1990–2019 |url=https://agerpres.ro/documentare/2024/11/21/prezidentiale2024-alegerile-prezidentiale-din-romania-perioada-1990-2019--1390889 |website=AGERPRES |date=2024-11-21 |language=ro |access-date=2026-07-16}}</ref>

== Background ==
[[Klaus Iohannis]]  won the [[2014 Romanian presidential election|previous presidential election]] in 2014 and was sworn in for his first term on 21 December 2014. According to the Article 83 of the [[Constitution of Romania]], the "term of office of the [[President of Romania]] is five years, being exercised from the date the oath was taken,"<ref>[[Constitution of Romania]], [http://www.cdep.ro/pls/dic/site.page?den=act2_2&par1=3#t3c2s0a81 Article 83] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180508185732/http://www.cdep.ro/pls/dic/site.page?den=act2_2&par1=3#t3c2s0a81 |date=2018-05-08 }}</ref> but only for up to two terms. In June 2018, incumbent president Iohannis publicly announced his intention of running for a second term as president.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/klaus-iohannis-a-anuntat-ca-va-candida-pentru-un-nou-mandat-de-presedinte-952012|title=Klaus Iohannis va candida pentru un nou mandat de președinte: "Sunt ferm hotărât"|work=digi24.ro|date=23 June 2018|access-date=23 June 2018|archive-date=23 June 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180623124450/https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/klaus-iohannis-a-anuntat-ca-va-candida-pentru-un-nou-mandat-de-presedinte-952012|url-status=live}}</ref> The electoral calendar for the presidential elections was set by the [[Government of Romania|Romanian Government]].

The final results for the first round were publicly announced by Central Electoral Bureau and Permanent Electoral Authority on 14 November 2019. The results were forwarded to the [[Constitutional Court of Romania]] that validated the results on 15 November 2019.<ref name="auto1">{{cite web|url=https://www.news.ro/politic-intern/curtea-constitutionala-a-validat-rezultatul-primului-tur-al-alegerilor-prezidentiale-zece-contestatii-care-au-vizat-alegerile-au-fost-depuse-toate-fiind-respinse-1922401915002019111419171742|title=Curtea Constituţională a validat rezultatul primului tur al alegerilor prezidenţiale; zece contestaţii care au vizat alegerile au fost depuse, toate fiind respinse|website=News.ro|date=15 November 2019 |access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 15, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191115160923/https://www.news.ro/politic-intern/curtea-constitutionala-a-validat-rezultatul-primului-tur-al-alegerilor-prezidentiale-zece-contestatii-care-au-vizat-alegerile-au-fost-depuse-toate-fiind-respinse-1922401915002019111419171742|url-status=live}}</ref> After the Constitutional Court's validation, the results were sent for publication to the Official Journal of Romania (''Monitorul Oficial al României''). Only after the publication by the Official Journal, the results for the first round of the elections became official.

The Central Electoral Bureau (BEC) forwarded the final results for the second round to the [[Constitutional Court of Romania]] for validation on 28 November 2019, on the last day of the settled electoral calendar.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.agerpres.ro/documentare/2019/11/11/calendarul-electoral-dupa-primul-tur-al-alegerilor-prezidentiale--400846|title=Calendarul electoral după primul tur al alegerilor prezidenţiale|website=www.agerpres.ro|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 12, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191112183128/https://www.agerpres.ro/documentare/2019/11/11/calendarul-electoral-dupa-primul-tur-al-alegerilor-prezidentiale--400846|url-status=live}}</ref> The [[Constitutional Court of Romania]] validated the results in the same day.<ref name="stirileprotv.ro">{{cite web|url=https://stirileprotv.ro/stiri/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019/ccr-a-validat-rezultatul-celui-de-al-doilea-tur-al-alegerilor-pentru-presedintele-romaniei.html|title=CCR a validat rezultatul alegerilor prezidențiale. Mesajul lui Iohannis pentru români|website=Stirileprotv.ro|access-date=2019-11-28|archive-date=2019-11-28|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191128161919/https://stirileprotv.ro/stiri/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019/ccr-a-validat-rezultatul-celui-de-al-doilea-tur-al-alegerilor-pentru-presedintele-romaniei.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

== Candidates ==
=== National Liberal Party (PNL) ===
President [[Klaus Iohannis]] was eligible for re-election. His candidacy in the [[2014 Romanian presidential election|2014 elections]] was supported by the [[National Liberal Party (Romania)|National Liberal Party]] (PNL), whose President he was at that time. Upon taking office as president, Iohannis suspended his PNL membership, as the Constitution does not allow the president to be a formal member of a political party during his term. [[Ludovic Orban]], the president of the PNL, reconfirmed the party's support for Iohannis after the elections.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Niculescu|first1=Anghel|title=Ludovic Orban a anunţat pe cine va susţine PNL la alegerile prezidenţiale din 2019! "Mă voi bate cu toată forţa mea să obţinem un nou mandat pentru Klaus Iohannis"|url=http://expressdebanat.ro/ludovic-orban-a-anuntat-pe-cine-va-sustine-pnl-la-alegerile-prezidentiale-din-2019-ma-voi-bate-cu-toata-forta-mea-sa-obtinem-un-nou-mandat-pentru-klaus-iohannis/|website=Express de Banat|access-date=4 August 2017|language=ro|date=2017-06-18|archive-date=2017-09-06|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170906225813/http://expressdebanat.ro/ludovic-orban-a-anuntat-pe-cine-va-sustine-pnl-la-alegerile-prezidentiale-din-2019-ma-voi-bate-cu-toata-forta-mea-sa-obtinem-un-nou-mandat-pentru-klaus-iohannis/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 11 March 2018, the National Council of PNL formally endorsed Klaus Iohannis for a new term as president.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://adevarul.ro/news/politica/conducerea-pnl-voteaza-sustinerea-presedintelui-iohannis-nou-mandat-orban-premier-1_5aa50844df52022f756ec670/index.html |title=Decizie PNL. Liberalii îl susţin pe Klaus Iohannis pentru un nou mandat de preşedinte. Ludovic Orban - premierul PNL |work=Adevărul |author=Sebastian Zachmann |date=11 March 2018 |language=ro |access-date=11 March 2018 |archive-date=11 March 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180311202206/http://adevarul.ro/news/politica/conducerea-pnl-voteaza-sustinerea-presedintelui-iohannis-nou-mandat-orban-premier-1_5aa50844df52022f756ec670/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== Social Democratic Party (PSD) ===
Liviu Pleșoianu, a member of the [[Chamber of Deputies of Romania|Chamber of Deputies]] for [[Bucharest]] since 2016 for the [[Social Democratic Party (Romania)|Social Democratic Party]] (PSD), declared his candidacy on 23 July 2017.<ref>{{cite web|title=Deputat PSD: Candidez la prezidențialele din 2019 (Video)|url=http://m.cotidianul.ro/deputat-psd-candidez-la-prezidentialele-din-2019-video-304291/|website=Cotidianul|access-date=4 August 2017|language=ro|date=2017-07-23|archive-date=2017-08-07|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170807070637/http://m.cotidianul.ro/deputat-psd-candidez-la-prezidentialele-din-2019-video-304291/|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Liviu Dragnea]], [[President of the Chamber of Deputies of Romania|President of the Chamber of Deputies]] since 2016,<ref>{{cite web|title=Olguța Vasilescu: Dragnea ar putea fi preşedinte|url=http://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/olguta-vasilescu-dragnea-ar-putea-fi-presedinte-711964|website=Digi24|date=25 April 2017 |access-date=4 August 2017|language=ro|archive-date=7 August 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170807021913/http://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/olguta-vasilescu-dragnea-ar-putea-fi-presedinte-711964|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last1=Pușcaș|first1=Florin|title=Dragnea nu respinge ideea unei candidaturi la prezidenţiale: 'Aş fi un preşedinte român'|url=http://www.stiripesurse.ro/dragnea-nu-respinge-ideea-unei-candidaturi-la-prezidentiale-as-fi-un-presedinte-roman_1196088.html|website=stiripesurse|date=14 May 2017 |access-date=4 August 2017|language=ro|archive-date=7 August 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170807022930/http://www.stiripesurse.ro/dragnea-nu-respinge-ideea-unei-candidaturi-la-prezidentiale-as-fi-un-presedinte-roman_1196088.html|url-status=live}}</ref> and [[Gabriela Firea]], [[Mayor of Bucharest]] since 2016, are thought to be other potential PSD candidates.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Leca|first1=Iulian|title=Firea, viitorul președinte?|url=http://www.ziare.com/gabriela-vranceanu-firea/primar-bucuresti/firea-viitorul-presedinte-1466178|website=Ziare.com|access-date=4 August 2017|language=ro|archive-date=7 August 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170807021551/http://www.ziare.com/gabriela-vranceanu-firea/primar-bucuresti/firea-viitorul-presedinte-1466178|url-status=live}}</ref> However, both have refuted these media speculations, Firea stating she wants to finish her term as mayor, while Liviu Dragnea rejected the idea and stated he and the PSD concentrate on the governing program and the parliamentary agenda, as Dragnea is President of the Chamber of Deputies. After being convicted on corruption charges on 27 May 2019, Dragnea became ineligible to run for president.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.euronews.com/2019/05/27/liviu-dragnea-romania-s-most-powerful-politician-sentenced-to-jail-for-corruption |title=Liviu Dragnea, Romania's most powerful politician, sentenced to jail for corruption |work=Euronews |date=27 May 2019 |access-date=27 May 2019 |archive-date=27 May 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190527122208/https://www.euronews.com/2019/05/27/liviu-dragnea-romania-s-most-powerful-politician-sentenced-to-jail-for-corruption |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== Save Romania Union (USR) and PLUS Alliance ===
[[Nicușor Dan]], a former President of the [[Save Romania Union]] (USR), the third largest political party in the country, believed that the party should run its own candidate for the elections.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://evz.ro/posibil-candidat-surpriza-2019.html |title=Posibil Candidat surpriză la Alegerile din 2019 |work=Evenimentul zilei |author=Andrei Marian |date=August 9, 2017 |language=ro |access-date=September 30, 2017 |archive-date=September 30, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170930175806/http://evz.ro/posibil-candidat-surpriza-2019.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Dan Barna, the new President of the USR, stated in an interview with ''[[Adevărul]]'' that the USR would have a presidential candidate, decided by a vote within the party. Barna also said that "[[Dacian Cioloș]] may be an option, like any well-known person".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-22283636-dan-barna-usr-avea-candidat-prezidentiale-decis-referendum-cadrul-partidului-dacian-ciolos-poate-varianta.htm |title=Dan Barna: USR va avea candidat la prezidențiale, decis de un referendum în cadrul partidului. Dacian Cioloș poate fi o variantă |work=HotNews |author=Alina Neagu |date=13 February 2018 |access-date=7 March 2018 |archive-date=8 March 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180308041409/https://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-22283636-dan-barna-usr-avea-candidat-prezidentiale-decis-referendum-cadrul-partidului-dacian-ciolos-poate-varianta.htm |url-status=live }}</ref>

Former Minister of Labor in [[Cioloș Cabinet|Cioloș Government]], Dragoș Pîslaru, who is among the founders of the new party of former Prime Minister, the [[Freedom, Unity and Solidarity Party|PLUS]], said the party was ready for a possible candidacy for the presidency of leader [[Dacian Cioloș]].<ref name="ciolos">{{cite web |url=https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/si-daca-ar-candida-si-ciolos-si-iohannis-ce-spune-dragos-pislaru-sustinator-al-fostului-premier-937201 |title=Și dacă ar candida și Cioloș, și Iohannis? Ce spune Dragoș Pîslaru, susținător al fostului premier |work=[[Digi24]] |date=28 May 2018 |language=ro |access-date=28 May 2018 |archive-date=28 May 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180528094317/https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/si-daca-ar-candida-si-ciolos-si-iohannis-ce-spune-dragos-pislaru-sustinator-al-fostului-premier-937201 |url-status=live }}</ref> He also stressed that a candidacy of President Iohannis for a new term would not exclude a candidacy of [[Dacian Cioloș]].<ref name="ciolos" /> On 8 June 2018, Cioloș said he would not run against Klaus Iohannis.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://adevarul.ro/news/politica/ciolos-nu-candida-iohannis-1_5b1ac3e2df52022f75ef0c8b/index.html |title=Cioloș: Nu voi candida împotriva lui Iohannis la prezidențiale |work=Adevărul |author=Radu Eremia |date=8 June 2018 |language=ro |access-date=8 June 2018 |archive-date=12 June 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180612143727/http://adevarul.ro/news/politica/ciolos-nu-candida-iohannis-1_5b1ac3e2df52022f75ef0c8b/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref> However he subsequently stated that he would assume any responsibility that his recently founded political party (PLUS) would bestow upon him, not excluding the presidency.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/ce-spune-ciolos-despre-o-eventuala-candidatura-la-prezidentiale-969855 |title=Ce spune Cioloş despre o eventuală candidatură la prezidenţiale |publisher=Digi24.ro |date=2018-07-25 |access-date=2019-10-16 |archive-date=2020-05-20 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200520113158/https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/ce-spune-ciolos-despre-o-eventuala-candidatura-la-prezidentiale-969855 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In the aftermath of the results of the 2019 European Parliament elections, USR and PLUS decided to keep the [[USR PLUS|2020 USR-PLUS Alliance]] for the presidential elections, and nominated [[Dan Barna]] as joint candidate.{{Citation needed|date=November 2019}}

=== Other political parties ===
Many voices inside [[Alliance of Liberals and Democrats (Romania)|ALDE]] suggested that [[Călin Popescu-Tăriceanu]], the party leader and former [[President of the Senate of Romania|President of the Senate]], should be the proposal of the PSD–ALDE coalition for the upcoming election and asked for PSD support in this regard.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.antena3.ro/politica/tariceanu-se-incalzeste-pentru-prezidentiale-alde-analizeaza-sondaje-pentru-cotroceni-464096.html |title=Tăriceanu se încălzește pentru prezidențiale. ALDE analizează sondaje pentru Cotroceni |work=Antena 3 |date=10 April 2018 |language=ro |access-date=20 May 2018 |archive-date=21 May 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180521104126/https://www.antena3.ro/politica/tariceanu-se-incalzeste-pentru-prezidentiale-alde-analizeaza-sondaje-pentru-cotroceni-464096.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Tăriceanu himself considered that the best option for the presidential election is a PSD–ALDE joint candidacy.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/tariceanu-despre-varianta-optima-la-alegerile-prezidentiale-923670 |title=Tăriceanu, despre "varianta optimă" la alegerile prezidențiale |work=Digi24 |date=4 May 2018 |language=ro |access-date=20 May 2018 |archive-date=21 May 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180521104122/https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/tariceanu-despre-varianta-optima-la-alegerile-prezidentiale-923670 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 24 July 2019, ALDE announced that Tăriceanu would run for president on its ticket.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-23275387-tariceanu-desemnat-candidatul-alde-prezidentiale.htm|title=''Tăriceanu, desemnat candidatul ALDE la prezidențiale: În acest moment în PSD bântuie un sentiment defetist, și anume își propun mult prea puțin. Candidatura Vioricăi Dăncilă, o dezamăgire''|newspaper=Hotnews|date=24 July 2019|access-date=24 July 2019|language=ro|archive-date=24 July 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190724143449/https://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-23275387-tariceanu-desemnat-candidatul-alde-prezidentiale.htm|url-status=live}}</ref>

In a press conference on 26 October 2017, [[Victor Ponta]], a former Prime Minister and runner-up in the [[2014 Romanian presidential election|2014 elections]], claimed that his newly established party, [[PRO Romania]], would nominate a candidate in the elections, but denied that he would run for the presidency again.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.dcnews.ro/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019-ponta-pro-romania-va-avea-un-candidat_563438.html |title=Alegeri prezidenţiale 2019. Ponta: Pro România va avea un candidat |work=DC News |author=Rodica Mitu |date=26 October 2017 |language=ro |access-date=5 March 2018 |archive-date=6 March 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180306023618/https://www.dcnews.ro/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019-ponta-pro-romania-va-avea-un-candidat_563438.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 25 August 2019, [[Theodor Paleologu]] was designated candidate of the [[People's Movement Party]] (PMP).<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-23330252-paleologu-dupa-presedintele-jucator-presedintele-spectato-nevoie-presedinte-invatator.htm|title=''Paleologu: După președintele jucător și președintele spectator, e nevoie de un președinte învățător'' ["Paleologu: After the player-president and the spectator-president, a teacher-president is needed"]|date=25 August 2019|access-date=25 August 2019|language=ro|archive-date=25 August 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190825131229/https://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-23330252-paleologu-dupa-presedintele-jucator-presedintele-spectato-nevoie-presedinte-invatator.htm|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 7 July 2019, Ramona-Ioana Bruynseels launched her candidacy.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/ramona-ioana-bruynseels-si-a-lansat-oficial-candidatura-la-prezidentiale-2689083|title=Ramona Ioana Bruynseels și-a lansat oficial candidatura la prezidențiale|date=2019-07-07|website=Libertatea|language=ro|access-date=2019-08-09|archive-date=2019-08-09|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190809085519/https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/ramona-ioana-bruynseels-si-a-lansat-oficial-candidatura-la-prezidentiale-2689083|url-status=live}}</ref> The announcement was met with surprise and intrigue from political commentators.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.jurnaldedambovita.ro/jdb_articol--surpriza-la-prezidentiale-ramona-ioana,49965.html|title=Surpriză la prezidenţiale: Ramona Ioana :: Jurnal de Dambovita|website=jurnaldedambovita.ro|access-date=2019-08-09|archive-date=2019-08-09|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190809085522/https://www.jurnaldedambovita.ro/jdb_articol--surpriza-la-prezidentiale-ramona-ioana,49965.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Bruynseels has set her platform on taking on the broken political system in Romania that she argues is working against the interests of its citizens.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ramonapresedinte.ro/viziunea-mea/|title=Viziunea mea|website=Ramona Presedinte|language=ro-RO|access-date=2019-08-09|archive-date=2019-10-31|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191031144624/https://ramonapresedinte.ro/viziunea-mea/|url-status=dead}}</ref> Bruynseels is a centrist politician and was the candidate of the [[Humanist Power Party]]. At the time of these elections, the party was controlled from behind the scenes by Romanian mogul and former longtime [[Securitate]]a collaborator [[Dan Voiculescu]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://adevarul.ro/news/politica/prima-femeie-intrat-cursa-cotroceni-ramona-ioana-bruynseels-candidata-partidului-controlat-voiculescu-1_5cfbf922892c0bb0c6236a8a/index.html |title=Ramona Ioana Bruynseels, 