== Campaign ==
The electoral campaign for the first round started on 12 October 2019, 0:00 [[Eastern European Time|EET]] and ended on 9 November 2019, 7:00 [[Eastern European Time|EET]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rfi.ro/politica-113861-guvernul-aprobat-calendarul-la-prezidentiale-campania-electorala-incepe-pe-12|title=Guvernul a aprobat calendarul pentru prezidențiale. Campania electorală începe pe 12 octombrie|date=Aug 27, 2019|website=RFI România: Actualitate, informaţii, ştiri în direct|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=October 22, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191022114931/https://www.rfi.ro/politica-113861-guvernul-aprobat-calendarul-la-prezidentiale-campania-electorala-incepe-pe-12|url-status=live}}</ref> The electoral campaign for the second round started on 15 November 2019, 0:00 [[Eastern European Time|EET]] (several hours before the first round results were validated by the Constitutional Court of Romania) and ended on 23 November 2019, 7:00 [[Eastern European Time|EET]]. According to Romanian law, both campaigns must end at least 24 hours before the official poll openings.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019-calendarul-procesului-electoral-1196994|title=Alegeri prezidențiale 2019. Azi începe campania electorală: Calendarul procesului electoral|website=www.digi24.ro|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 3, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191103154114/https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019-calendarul-procesului-electoral-1196994|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Controversies===
The candidate [[Dan Barna]] did not comply with the legal requirements regarding the mention of a candidate's first-degree relatives income, in the public declaration of assets (document required in a candidate's file, while registering at the Electoral Board). He stated that his wife income - who was at the time employed at [[Petrom]] - was "classified". Soon after the story sparked, he declassified his wife's annual income and changed his assets statement.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.g4media.ro/dan-barna-a-facut-publice-veniturile-sotiei-sale-desi-anterior-le-a-anonimizat-in-declaratia-de-avere-depusa-la-bec.html|title=Dan Barna a făcut publice veniturile soției sale, deși anterior le-a anonimizat în declarația de avere depusă la BEC|date=Sep 26, 2019|website=G4Media|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=September 13, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200913013638/https://www.g4media.ro/dan-barna-a-facut-publice-veniturile-sotiei-sale-desi-anterior-le-a-anonimizat-in-declaratia-de-avere-depusa-la-bec.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

According to a media investigation, [[Dan Barna]] was allegedly involved in a financial scheme during his entrepreneurship time. He rejected the allegations.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.riseproject.ro/articol/adevarul-despre-dan-barna/|title=Adevărul despre Dan Barna|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 12, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201112015252/https://www.riseproject.ro/articol/adevarul-despre-dan-barna/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Media released recordings of conversations that the candidate Ramona-Ioana Bruynseels had with her staff, regarding allegedly dubious acts committed with her campaign funds by [[Dan Voiculescu]], the informal leader of the party that supports her candidacy.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://newsweek.ro/investigatii/exclusiv-audio-candidata-lui-voiculescu-il-acuza-pe-varan-de-santaj-si-furt-de-bani-de-campanie|title=EXCLUSIV AUDIO Candidata lui Voiculescu îl acuză pe "varan" de șantaj și furt de bani de campanie &#124; Newsweek Romania|website=newsweek.ro|date=17 October 2019 |access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 23, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191123094919/https://newsweek.ro/investigatii/exclusiv-audio-candidata-lui-voiculescu-il-acuza-pe-varan-de-santaj-si-furt-de-bani-de-campanie|url-status=live}}</ref>

The candidate [[:ro:Ninel Peia|Ninel Peia]] was reported missing, during the night of 6–7 November 2019. He was seen leaving the hotel he was lodging in [[Cluj-Napoca]], at 1:17 am, and did not return.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-esential-23475411-alerta-disparut-candidat-prezidentiale-ninel-peia-plecat-azi-noapte-hotel-nu-mai-putut-contactat.htm|title=Alertă: A dispărut un candidat la prezidențiale / Ninel Peia a plecat azi noapte de la hotel și nu a mai putut fi contactat - Esential - HotNews.ro|date=Nov 7, 2019|website=www.hotnews.ro|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 15, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191115164344/https://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-esential-23475411-alerta-disparut-candidat-prezidentiale-ninel-peia-plecat-azi-noapte-hotel-nu-mai-putut-contactat.htm|url-status=live}}</ref> The following morning, he was found at [[Putna Monastery]], 195&nbsp;km away, stating that he went there "to pray".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/ninel-peia-a-fost-gasit-2794486|title=Ninel Peia a fost găsit la Mănăstirea Putna, unde a mers să se roage|date=Nov 8, 2019|website=Libertatea|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 16, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191116034315/https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/ninel-peia-a-fost-gasit-2794486|url-status=live}}</ref>

The candidate [[Viorel Cataramă]] was reported as a former informer of the infamous Securitate (Communist Romania's intelligence service). He rejected the allegations.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.mediafax.ro/politic/catarama-voi-cere-la-cnsas-documentele-originale-despre-care-vorbesc-e-un-atac-pe-stiri-false-18553912|title=Cataramă: Voi cere la CNSAS documentele originale despre care vorbesc. E un atac pe ştiri false|website=Mediafax.ro|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 8, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191108161414/https://www.mediafax.ro/politic/catarama-voi-cere-la-cnsas-documentele-originale-despre-care-vorbesc-e-un-atac-pe-stiri-false-18553912|url-status=live}}</ref>

Alexandru Cumpănașu was accused of either forging his BA degree or lying about being a university graduate. He failed to show a Bachelor's degree, while stating that he was a university graduate, without mentioning a university or faculty. He publicly showed an honorary diploma issued by a controversial university of Ukraine, but failed to prove his claimed status of a university graduate. Later on, he mentioned in the documents filed at the Electoral Bureau that he only graduated high-school and did not pursued any university studies. Asked to clear his lack of university studies required for a Master's degree or a Doctor degree, he stated "In my opinion, I pursued university studies".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.digifm.ro/stiri/cumpanasu-nu-a-absolvit-facultatea-dar-are-titlu-de-doctor-honoris-causa-52063|title=Cumpănașu nu a absolvit facultatea, dar are titlu de Doctor Honoris Causa|website=www.digifm.ro|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=December 11, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191211200905/https://www.digifm.ro/stiri/cumpanasu-nu-a-absolvit-facultatea-dar-are-titlu-de-doctor-honoris-causa-52063|url-status=live}}</ref>

A radio anchor that hosted a live debate warned the candidate Alexandru Cumpănașu to tone down his language, or else he would be facing exclusion from the debate.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://magnanews.ro/2019/10/cumpanasu-era-sa-fie-dat-afara-din-studio-la-radio-romania-actualitati/|title=Cumpănaşu era să fie dat afară din studio, la Radio România Actualităţi|first=Anca|last=Apostol|date=October 16, 2019|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 7, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191107200515/https://magnanews.ro/2019/10/cumpanasu-era-sa-fie-dat-afara-din-studio-la-radio-romania-actualitati/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In an electoral show broadcast live by the Romanian public TV station [[TVR1]], Alexandru Cumpănașu showed his skills of gun handling, by firing at sitting balloons. Later, he stated that the submachine gun he used "was a toy-gun".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019/alexandru-cumpanasu-cu-arma-in-studioul-tvr-ce-transmite-acest-gest-in-campania-electorala-1211073|title=Alexandru Cumpănașu, cu arma în studioul TVR. Ce transmite acest gest în campania electorală?|website=www.digi24.ro|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 7, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191107200522/https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/alegeri-prezidentiale-2019/alexandru-cumpanasu-cu-arma-in-studioul-tvr-ce-transmite-acest-gest-in-campania-electorala-1211073|url-status=live}}</ref>

For the first time in the history of democratic elections in Romania, the first two contenders did not participate in any electoral debate organised between them or together with other candidates.

