This is an overview of the money raised by each candidate, as it was reported to the Permanent Electoral Authority.<ref name=":0" /> Total raised are the sum of all contributions (private and public).

====First round====
For the first round, the candidates raised a total of 70,258,904.02 lei, including both private and public funding.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |url=https://finantarepartide.ro/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/5.-SITE-Declarare-contributii-prezidentiale-14.11.-2019.pdf |title=Archived copy |access-date=2019-11-14 |archive-date=2019-11-14 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191114195824/https://finantarepartide.ro/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/5.-SITE-Declarare-contributii-prezidentiale-14.11.-2019.pdf |url-status=live }}</ref> Only the candidates that achieved at least 3% of the votes were entitled to be compensated for their private fundings from the state budget. According to Romanian law, the candidates that achieved less than 3% (highlighted in red, in the table below) are not entitled to public compensations. One candidate, Sebastian Popescu, claimed in his financial filing that he and his team did not spend any funds, saying that he used only the online environment for his campaign and no paid ads.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rfi.ro/politica-115553-sebastian-popescu-schimbare-clasa-politica|title=(VIDEO) Candidatul la Președinție Sebastian Popescu: Vreau schimbarea clasei politice, dar nu cu cătușe, ci prin vot|date=Oct 31, 2019|website=RFI România: Actualitate, informaţii, ştiri în direct|access-date=Nov 24, 2019|archive-date=November 16, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191116193201/https://www.rfi.ro/politica-115553-sebastian-popescu-schimbare-clasa-politica|url-status=live}}</ref>

